The attached image (Figure 2) illustrates the in vivo distribution and clearance kinetics of Nano-11 nanoparticles in mice over a 3-week period. Panel A shows whole-mouse fluorescence imaging, demonstrating that Alexa Fluor 647-labeled Nano-11 remains localized at the intramuscular injection site and gradually clears over time. Panel B confirms, through ex vivo imaging of excised organs at day 21, that Nano-11 does not systemically distribute to internal organs but remains at the injection site. Panel C quantifies the injection site fluorescence, showing a rapid decrease by day 1, a transient increase by day 2, and then a steady decline, with only ~20% of the initial signal remaining by day 21, indicating local retention and eventual clearance.